.TH TULPAR 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar \- package manager frontend for NurOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tulpar
is the command-line package manager for NurOS. It resolves, downloads,
installs, removes, and upgrades packages, backed by libapg for local
package database and transaction handling and by a Tulpar Server
instance for remote repository operations.
.PP
Every command has three equivalent invocation forms: a full name, a
single-letter short alias used as the first word, and the same letter
used as a leading flag. The following are identical:
.PP
.RS
tulpar install curl
.br
tulpar i curl
.br
tulpar \-i curl
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR tulpar-install (1)
install one or more packages
.TP
.BR tulpar-remove (1)
remove an installed package (also: uninstall)
.TP
.BR tulpar-upgrade (1)
upgrade one or all installed packages
.TP
.BR tulpar-search (1)
search local and remote package indexes
.TP
.BR tulpar-list (1)
list installed packages
.TP
.BR tulpar-info (1)
show full metadata for a package (also: show)
.TP
.BR tulpar-verify (1)
verify installed package files
.TP
.BR tulpar-orphans (1)
list and remove orphaned packages (also: autoremove)
.TP
.BR tulpar-hold (1)
block a package from upgrade or removal
.TP
.BR tulpar-unhold (1)
release a held package
.TP
.BR tulpar-history (1)
show past install/remove operations (also: audit, log)
.TP
.BR tulpar-repo (1)
manage configured repositories
.TP
.BR tulpar-download (1)
fetch a package without installing it
.TP
.BR tulpar-key (1)
manage the trusted signing keyring
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the tulpar version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes and skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Produce machine-readable JSON output, where supported.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate against an alternate filesystem root instead of the live
system. The package database is resolved under
.IR path /var/lib/apg/db
and no root privileges are required, since the destination may be
user-owned.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress informational output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Reject packages that fail signature verification instead of only
warning about them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apg/tulpar.conf
System-wide configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/tulpar.conf
Per-user configuration overrides.
.TP
.I /etc/apg/repos
System-wide repository list.
.TP
.I ~/.config/apg/repos
Per-user repository list.
.TP
.I /var/cache/apg/pkgs/
Downloaded package cache.
.TP
.I /var/cache/apg/repodata/
Cached repository indexes.
.TP
.I /var/log/tulpar.log
Default log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar.conf (5),
.BR tulpar-install (1),
.BR tulpar-repo (1)
